# 1. Basic structure: pattern { action }, once per line
# An awk program is a list of rules. Each rule is a pattern and an action in braces.
# No pattern means "every line". awk splits each line into fields: $1, $2, ... $9 here.
# Our data is a directory listing: the file name is the 9th field.
# Try: change $9 to $5 to print sizes instead, then save.
{ print "file:", $9 }

